<section id="how-start" class="container how-path-section" aria-labelledby="path-title"><div class="how-section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">START WITH THE DATA YOU HAVE</span><h2 id="path-title">Two paths into the same workspace.</h2><p>Monthly bills and interval readings answer different questions. You can add either or both to a building.</p></div><div class="how-path-grid"><article class="how-path-card how-path-bills"><div class="how-path-card-head"><i class="fa-solid fa-receipt" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>PATH 01 / MONTHLY BILLS</span></div><h3>Understand spending over time.</h3><p>Enter each bill’s period, kWh, and amount. Once you have two months, Caldren shows how usage and spending changed.</p><div class="how-path-visual obs-light-glass"><div><small>MONTHLY AMOUNT · EXAMPLE</small><strong>USD 190.00</strong></div><div class="how-path-bars" aria-hidden="true"><span style="height:48%"></span><span style="height:64%"></span><span style="height:55%"></span><span style="height:82%"></span></div></div><small class="how-path-foot">Bill-only buildings do not produce a demand forecast.</small></article><article class="how-path-card how-path-readings"><div class="how-path-card-head"><i class="fa-solid fa-wave-square" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>PATH 02 / INTERVAL READINGS</span></div><h3>See when demand occurs.</h3><p>Upload a CSV with <code>timestamp,kwh</code> columns. Caldren validates timestamps and kWh values and rejects duplicate timestamps in the file.</p><div class="how-path-visual obs-light-glass"><div><small>CSV FORMAT · EXAMPLE</small><strong>timestamp,kwh</strong></div><code>2026-10-01 09:00,42.6<br>2026-10-01 10:00,45.1</code></div><small class="how-path-foot">Recent, well-covered readings can unlock a seven-day outlook.</small></article></div></section>

<section class="how-process-wrap" aria-labelledby="process-title"><div class="container"><div class="how-section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">THE WORKFLOW</span><h2 id="process-title">A practical path from setup to review.</h2><p>Each step keeps the building context and the limitations of the data visible.</p></div><div class="how-process-list"><article class="how-process-step"><div class="how-process-copy"><span class="how-step-number">01 / SET UP</span><h3>Create a home for your buildings.</h3><p>Create an organization, add each building’s location and time zone, and set its standard energy rate. Peak rate and hours can be added when relevant. A workspace owner can invite teammates.</p></div><div class="how-step-art how-step-portfolio"><div class="how-step-glass obs-light-glass"><span>EXAMPLE ORGANIZATION</span><div><i class="fa-solid fa-building" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>Building A</strong><small>Time zone · tariff</small></div><div><i class="fa-solid fa-building" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>Building B</strong><small>Time zone · tariff</small></div><div><i class="fa-solid fa-building" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>Building C</strong><small>Time zone · tariff</small></div></div></div></article><article class="how-process-step reverse"><div class="how-process-copy"><span class="how-step-number">02 / IMPORT</span><h3>Bring in the energy history.</h3><p>Upload interval readings or record monthly bills for the right building. The CSV import checks formatting and values before saving readings. Forecasting checks recent coverage separately when you request an outlook.</p></div><div class="how-step-art how-step-import"><div class="how-import-file"><div><i class="fa-solid fa-file-csv" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>readings.csv</span><small>EXAMPLE FILE</small></div><code>timestamp,kwh<br>2026-10-01 09:00,42.6<br>2026-10-01 10:00,45.1</code></div><div class="how-import-status obs-light-glass"><i class="fa-solid fa-check" aria-hidden="true"></i> Timestamp and kWh checked</div></div></article><article class="how-process-step"><div class="how-process-copy"><span class="how-step-number">03 / ESTIMATE</span><h3>Review the next seven days.</h3><p>With at least 14 complete days of recent hourly or sub-hourly readings and sufficient daily coverage, request daily energy and peak estimates. Caldren shows the input period and historical baseline beside the result.</p><p class="how-process-note">The estimate is checked for plausible values. If generation fails, your historical data remains available and you can retry.</p></div><div class="how-step-art how-step-forecast"><div class="how-forecast-glass observatory-glass"><span>SEVEN-DAY OUTLOOK · ILLUSTRATIVE</span><div class="how-forecast-days"><div><small>MON</small><strong>5.2</strong></div><div><small>TUE</small><strong>5.8</strong></div><div class="active"><small>WED</small><strong>6.1</strong></div><div><small>THU</small><strong>5.6</strong></div><div><small>FRI</small><strong>5.4</strong></div><div><small>SAT</small><strong>4.7</strong></div><div><small>SUN</small><strong>4.5</strong></div></div><div class="how-forecast-baseline">Historical baseline <strong>5.1 MWh/day</strong></div></div></div></article><article class="how-process-step reverse"><div class="how-process-copy"><span class="how-step-number">04 / REVIEW</span><h3>Turn the outlook into a conversation.</h3><p>Consider possible peak alerts and tariff-aware opportunities with your facility team. Compare estimates with actual conditions and operating constraints before changing schedules or equipment settings.</p></div><div class="how-step-art how-step-review"><div class="how-review-card obs-light-glass"><span><i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation" aria-hidden="true"></i> POSSIBLE PEAK · EXAMPLE</span><strong>Review afternoon demand</strong><p>Check flexible loads during the expected peak window.</p></div><div class="how-review-card obs-light-glass"><span><i class="fa-solid fa-users" aria-hidden="true"></i> TEAM DISCUSSION</span><strong>Agree on the next check</strong><p>Use building knowledge to evaluate the suggestion.</p></div></div></article></div></div></section>

<section class="how-context-section" aria-labelledby="context-title"><div class="container how-context-layout"><div><span class="obs-kicker">ESTIMATES WITH CONTEXT</span><h2 id="context-title">Know what the outlook is based on.</h2><p>Caldren sends bounded daily usage summaries and tariff settings to the configured AI service. It checks the returned seven-day estimate against the historical baseline before showing it to your team.</p><a class="obs-outline-button" href="{{ route('privacy') }}">Read the privacy details</a></div><div class="how-context-chain"><div class="observatory-glass"><i class="fa-solid fa-database" aria-hidden="true"></i><span><strong>Recent history</strong><small>14 complete days of interval data</small></span></div><div class="observatory-glass"><i class="fa-solid fa-chart-line" aria-hidden="true"></i><span><strong>Checked estimate</strong><small>Seven daily energy and peak values</small></span></div><div class="observatory-glass"><i class="fa-solid fa-user-check" aria-hidden="true"></i><span><strong>Human review</strong><small>Compare with actual conditions</small></span></div></div></div></section>

